#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""scorecard runner: measure one pinned commit of a subject repo against the seven ideals and print ONE JSON card (scorecard/SPEC.md, scorecard/DECISIONS.md).
  scorecard/scorecard run --repo <path> --commit <rev> [--adapter <file>] [--out <file>] [--sandbox <launcher>] [--keep]
The subject is UNTRUSTED CODE (scorecard/SPEC.md): it is only READ, in a scratch CLONE (removed afterwards), and NOTHING of it is executed unless a sandbox launcher is given (--sandbox) and its attestation checks out.
Static metrics read only files the adapter declares, through one guard (no symlinks, no `..`, size-capped) and under an alarm (adapter regexes are hostile). The adapter defaults to scorecard.toml at the pinned commit. A missing, unknown or mistyped adapter key is
rejected (exit 2). Floors, no averaging: a dimension with a floored metric that is `fail` or `not-measurable` fails; one failing dimension fails the card. `result` is strict (a metric this runner does
not implement is not-measurable and fails its floor); `implemented_result` judges only the implemented metrics. Same commits in, same bytes out: no clock value appears in the card except the measured seconds, and every such metric is marked `measured: true` (it varies with load; scripts/test_scorecard.sh compares runs with those values masked).
The metric table below, the floors and the adapter schema are gate-defining (scripts/protected-paths.txt)."""
